    <member name="M:System.Math.Atan(System.Double)">
      <summary>Returns the angle whose tangent is the specified number.</summary>
      <param name="d">A number representing a tangent.</param>
      <returns>An angle, Œ∏, measured in radians, such that -œÄ/2 ‚â§Œ∏‚â§œÄ/2.  
 -or-  
 <see cref="F:System.Double.NaN" /> if <paramref name="d" /> equals <see cref="F:System.Double.NaN" />, -œÄ/2 rounded to double precision (-1.5707963267949) if <paramref name="d" /> equals <see cref="F:System.Double.NegativeInfinity" />, or œÄ/2 rounded to double precision (1.5707963267949) if <paramref name="d" /> equals <see cref="F:System.Double.PositiveInfinity" />.</returns>
    </member>
    <member name="M:System.Math.Atan2(System.Double,System.Double)">
      <summary>Returns the angle whose tangent is the quotient of two specified numbers.</summary>
      <param name="y">The y coordinate of a point.</param>
      <param name="x">The x coordinate of a point.</param>
      <returns>An angle, Œ∏, measured in radians, such that -œÄ‚â§Œ∏‚â§œÄ, and tan(Œ∏) = <paramref name="y" /> / <paramref name="x" />, where (<paramref name="x" />, <paramref name="y" />) is a point in the Cartesian plane. Observe the following:  

For (<paramref name="x" />, <paramref name="y" />) in quadrant 1, 0 &lt; Œ∏ &lt; œÄ/2.  

For (<paramref name="x" />, <paramref name="y" />) in quadrant 2, œÄ/2 &lt; Œ∏‚â§œÄ.  

For (<paramref name="x" />, <paramref name="y" />) in quadrant 3, -œÄ &lt; Œ∏ &lt; -œÄ/2.  

For (<paramref name="x" />, <paramref name="y" />) in quadrant 4, -œÄ/2 &lt; Œ∏ &lt; 0.  


 For points on the boundaries of the quadrants, the return value is the following:  

If y is 0 and x is not negative, Œ∏ = 0.  

If y is 0 and x is negative, Œ∏ = œÄ.  

If y is positive and x is 0, Œ∏ = œÄ/2.  

If y is negative and x is 0, Œ∏ = -œÄ/2.  

If y is 0 and x is 0, Œ∏ = 0.  


 If <paramref name="x" /> or <paramref name="y" /> is <see cref="F:System.Double.NaN" />, or if <paramref name="x" /> and <paramref name="y" /> are either <see cref="F:System.Double.PositiveInfinity" /> or <see cref="F:System.Double.NegativeInfinity" />, the method returns <see cref="F:System.Double.NaN" />.</returns>
    </member>
